"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[27],{4941(e,a,t){t.r(a),t.d(a,{_pageData:()=>r,default:()=>o});var n=t(641);const r=JSON.parse('{"path":"/woocommerce-pre-order/campaigns.html","title":"Pre-Order Campaigns","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"woocommerce-pre-order/campaigns.md"}'),i={name:"campaigns.md"},o=(0,t(6262).A)(i,[["render",function(e,a,t,r,i,o){return(0,n.uX)(),(0,n.CE)("div",null,[...a[0]||(a[0]=[(0,n.Fv)('<h1 id="pre-order-campaigns" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#pre-order-campaigns"><span>Pre-Order Campaigns</span></a></h1><p>Pre-order campaigns allow merchants to run coordinated pre-sales for groups of products. You can schedule campaigns with start/end dates, set custom discount rules, and display the products on any storefront page using built-in shortcodes.</p><p>To manage campaigns, navigate to <strong>WooCommerce</strong> &gt; <strong>Pre-Order List</strong> and select the <strong>Pre-Order Campaigns</strong> tab.</p><hr><h2 id="_1-creating-a-campaign" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-creating-a-campaign"><span>1. Creating a Campaign</span></a></h2><p>Click <strong>Add New Campaign</strong> to open the Campaign Editor.</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-campaign-editor.png" alt="Admin Campaign Editor"></p><p>The editor is split into three configuration tabs:</p><h3 id="tab-a-general-information" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#tab-a-general-information"><span>Tab A: General Information</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Campaign Name:</strong> The internal name for the campaign (e.g., <em>“Fall Tech Launch 2026”</em>).</li><li><strong>Banner Text (Description):</strong> Promotional text displayed to customers. You can use dynamic merge tags in this block: <ul><li><code>{name}</code> — The Campaign Name.</li><li><code>{discount}</code> — The formatted discount amount (e.g. <em>15% off</em>).</li><li><code>{start_date}</code> — Formatted start date/time.</li><li><code>{end_date}</code> — Formatted end date/time.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Start &amp; End Dates:</strong> Enter local times for the campaign launch and closure. The plugin converts these inputs to UTC for precise scheduling.</li><li><strong>Shortcode:</strong> Once a campaign is saved, the editor displays its unique shortcode:<div class="language-text line-numbers-mode" data-highlighter="prismjs" data-ext="text"><pre><code class="language-text"><span class="line">[wk_campaign_products campaign_id=&quot;YOUR_CAMPAIGN_ID&quot;]</span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><div class="line-numbers" aria-hidden="true" style="counter-reset:line-number 0;"><div class="line-number"></div></div></div>Paste this shortcode on any WordPress page, Gutenberg block, or Elementor container to render the campaign product grid. The grid only displays while the campaign is actively running.</li></ul><h3 id="storefront-campaign-showcase" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#storefront-campaign-showcase"><span>Storefront Campaign Showcase</span></a></h3><p>Below is an example of an active pre-order campaign grid rendered on a storefront page built using Elementor, featuring the promotional banner text, countdown timer, and campaign-linked pre-order products:</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/front-end-campaign-view.png" alt="Frontend Pre-Order Campaign Grid Showcase"></p><h3 id="tab-b-discount-pricing" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#tab-b-discount-pricing"><span>Tab B: Discount &amp; Pricing</span></a></h3><p>Configure how the campaign&#39;s promotional pricing interacts with individual product catalog prices:</p><ul><li><strong>Discount Type:</strong> Choose <strong>Percentage</strong> or <strong>Fixed Amount</strong>.</li><li><strong>Discount Value:</strong> Enter the numerical value (e.g., <code>15</code> for a 15% markdown).</li><li><strong>Discount Precedence:</strong> If a product in the campaign already has a custom pre-order discount defined at the individual product level, determine which discount takes priority: <ul><li><strong>Higher Wins:</strong> The plugin compares the campaign discount and the per-product discount, applying whichever saves the customer more.</li><li><strong>Campaign Always Wins:</strong> The campaign discount overrides all product-level values.</li></ul></li></ul><h3 id="tab-c-products" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#tab-c-products"><span>Tab C: Products</span></a></h3><p>Attach or detach products to the campaign.</p><ul><li><strong>Add Products:</strong> Opens a search box powered by Select2. Search your WooCommerce catalog, select one or multiple products, and click <strong>Attach to Campaign</strong>.</li><li><strong>Remove Selected:</strong> Check the boxes next to assigned products and click to detach them.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="_2-campaign-states-lifecycle" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-campaign-states-lifecycle"><span>2. Campaign States &amp; Lifecycle</span></a></h2><p>A campaign shifts automatically through states based on its scheduled dates and active toggle status:</p><ul><li><strong>Draft:</strong> The campaign has been saved but is not active. Products do not show campaign pricing.</li><li><strong>Scheduled:</strong> Saved and activated, but the start date is in the future. Shop loop badges show &quot;PRE-ORDERS START SOON!&quot; to build anticipation.</li><li><strong>Active:</strong> The current date falls within the campaign schedule window. Campaign discounts are applied, and countdown timers are visible on product pages.</li><li><strong>Expired:</strong> The end date has passed. Pre-ordering automatically closes, returning items to their standard shop status.</li><li><strong>Disabled:</strong> Manually paused or turned off by the admin, pausing all campaign rules regardless of schedule.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="_3-sidebar-quick-metrics" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-sidebar-quick-metrics"><span>3. Sidebar Quick Metrics</span></a></h2><p>The right-hand sidebar of the Campaign Editor provides quick administrative oversight:</p><ul><li><strong>Campaign Status Pill:</strong> Color-coded indicator displaying the active status.</li><li><strong>Duration:</strong> The scheduled length of the campaign.</li><li><strong>Days Remaining:</strong> A real-time countdown of remaining days until expiration.</li><li><strong>Quick Stats:</strong> Total number of products currently assigned and the active discount rate.</li></ul>',27)])])}]])}}]);